\f0\fs24 \cf0 You are helping me build a digital version of the party game Scattergories. I need a large pool of family-friendly category names that players will get answers for (each answer must start with a chosen letter).\
\
Generate a JSON array of EXACTLY 300 unique category names, following these rules:\
\
DIFFICULTY MIX (roughly):\
- 40% easy (concrete, broad \'97 most players can think of several answers)\
- 40% medium (more specific, requires some thought)\
- 20% hard (narrow, clever, or unusual \'97 for variety)\
\
STRUCTURAL VARIETY (mix these patterns roughly evenly):\
- Simple nouns: "Animal", "Country", "Fruit"\
- "A type of X": "A type of cheese", "A type of dance"\
- "Things you find in X": "Things you find in a kitchen", "Things you find at the beach"\
- "Things that are X": "Things that are round", "Things that are sticky"\
- "Verbs/actions": "Something you do at a party", "Ways to travel"\
- "Famous X": "Famous scientists", "Famous bands"\
- "X with Y": "Foods with a hole", "Movies with a number in the title"\
- Compound/clever: "Things that come in pairs", "Words that rhyme with 'cat'"\
- Body/sensory: "Things that smell good", "Things you wear on your feet"\
- Pop culture: "TV shows", "Video game characters", "Board games"\
\
TOPIC COVERAGE (aim for spread across these):\
Food & drink, animals & nature, places & geography, household items, clothing & accessories, transport, sport & games, entertainment (TV/film/music/books), school subjects, jobs & professions, hobbies, science & tech, history, body & health, weather, emotions & abstract, holidays & celebrations, mythology, art & crafts, tools.\
\
RULES:\
- Family-friendly: no profanity, no adult themes, no political figures, no graphic content.\
- Universally understandable: avoid niche references only one country/culture would know. Mild UK bias is fine since the players are British, but skip overly local references.\
- Unique within this batch: no duplicates, no near-duplicates ("Types of dog" and "Dog breeds" are the same \'97 pick one).\
- Reasonable: every category must have at least 5\'9610 plausible answers across the alphabet. Skip categories where most letters would be impossible (e.g. "Words starting with Z that mean happy").\
- Phrase categories naturally as you'd see on the physical Scattergories card.\
- Avoid letter-locked categories ("Words starting with B") \'97 the letter is chosen separately at game time.\
\
OUTPUT FORMAT:\
Return ONLY a valid JSON array of strings. No preamble, no commentary, no markdown code fences, no numbering. Just the array. Example shape:\
\
["Animal", "A type of cheese", "Things you find in a kitchen", ...]}